Overpay and get the difference refunded!
Nanjing real estate market sees “difference compensation” again - ChinaNetNewsCenter
The Yangtze Evening Post/ZiNiu News (Reporter Ma Zuobow). On October 10th, during an interview, it was found that a long-missing "valuation agreement" has returned to the Nanjing real estate market. A property located in the New District of Jiangbei announced "price difference compensation," stating that other available units offer greater discounts than previous discounts prior to delivery, and that the developer is willing to swap houses and refund the price difference for buyers.
"Shipment Valuation Agreement" terms are not few
The property located in the New District of Jiangbei is called Poly Yanziyu Cloud Terrace. Mr. Sun, who was viewing the property, told the reporter that he found a "statement" last weekend when he was browsing the property.
The pictures sent to the journalists show that the developer of the楼盘 has promised that anyone who purchases a property unit between February 1st and February 28th will be eligible for a swap and receive a refund of the difference in price if other unsold properties within the project offer greater discounts than those they received when purchasing their unit (limited to other units of the same户型, in the same栋, in the same单元, and of the same物业类型 that have not been sold). This can be done from the date of signing the sales contract until the corresponding property is delivered.
Sun says real estate agents say it is essentially a “price-locking agreement” intended to give buyers peace of mind and prevent them from worrying about developers offering discounts or price cuts afterward. Now, what worries buyers most is that after they make the purchase, the developer might lower the price. Rushing to the sales office to protest won’t work, nor will staying quiet, as it would be very uncomfortable.
Yet, there are still many homebuyers who view "price stabilization agreements" as offering little more than a sense of security since the conditions are rather stringent.
Ms. Zheng, who plans to buy a starter home in North Jianghe, says that the price-protected listings must be of the same户型, and also in the same building and unit. With so few such listings available for comparison shopping, however, the “barrier” remains fairly high.
Also, some buyers argue that it is not easy for them to "protect their rights" during transactions due to asymmetry of information, as sellers may offer additional discounts outside of the public offer when there is none mentioned.
Whether they can retain home buyers remains to be seen.
The reporter found out from Nanjing Online Real Estate that the project obtained a sales permit for two buildings totaling 252 units last November, with户型sizes ranging from 105 sqm, 114 sqm, and 129 sqm, and the fully renovated selling price was 39,843 yuan per sqm.
However, in less than two months, online real estate shows that the total unsold units of the project currently stand at 157, accounting for 62.3%, with 128 units in Tower 8 having 113 unsold and 124 units in Tower 7 with 44 unsold. The total sold units account for only 33, making up 13% of the project.
Market participants explain that "price protection agreements" also appeared in Nanjing in 2008.
In August of that year, the housing project Xiangtang Xiyuan on Huangshan Road West in Heguo launched the "Price Guarantee Plan" to attract homebuyers. The specifics of the plan were as follows: "The company solemnly commits that if the project offers further discounts within a year, the difference will be refunded to the original owners by the company."
Subsequently in April 2011, nine housing projects in Nanjing also offered some units for sale with a “price differential compensation” commitment.
The real estate market is warming up, and now more than ever requires a ‘shot of adrenaline.’
Mr. Shen, a seasoned operator in the Nanjing real estate industry, stated that “price protection agreements” are also one of the marketing strategies for房企.
He believes that enterprises need more confidence than homebuyers at the moment, and launching a "price guarantee agreement" is actually boosting their morale.
Regarding whether he can retain homebuyers, he notes that it depends on multiple factors such as regulatory policies and loan thresholds, and it remains to be seen at this time.
Chinese rescue teams continue to carry out rescue operations in Turkey and have rescued four trapped individuals - Xinhua.
Xinhua News Agency报道，according to the website of the Ministry of Emergency Management on February 11th, on February 10th, the Chinese rescue team currently searching for survivors in Turkey dispatched three operational teams and 45 rescue personnel, rescuing one trapped person.
Dispatched two search assessment teams to evaluate and investigate 15 buildings on Vodabash Street.
To date, four trapped individuals have been rescued, five fatalities have been identified, and life signs and risks assessments have been conducted on 25 severely damaged buildings.
The rescue forces will adjust their rescue efforts scientifically based on the actual conditions of the disaster area and the site, and continue to conduct rescue operations in depth.
The rescue teams obtain rescue求助 information through various channels such as embassies, local governments, and UN relief organizations, and verify each case through multiple methods including online inquiries and on-site searches.
Introduce the current rescue environment and building collapse situations to the Chinese Hong Kong Rescuing Team, and conduct joint search operations.
Currently serving as the Regional Coordination System (SSC5) with the Italian rescue team, and dispatching three members to work at the 5th RescEU Coordination Center. Communicating with multiple teams from countries including Italy, the United Kingdom, Serbia, Slovakia, and Oman, I have gained an understanding of the rescue operations conducted by both the UN rescue organization and various national rescue teams.
The rescue team continues to reinforce safety management and force support, adhering to the principle of "unified command, safety first," strengthening safety control at the rescue site, and enhancing requirements for rescue work discipline. Safety precautions are also clearly defined.
Implement continuous rotation on-duty and sentry work systems to strengthen camp security management.
Medical personnel of the rescue team provide daily health check-ups for the members to enhance medical safeguards for key personnel. Currently, all members of the rescue team are in good health, and they are conducting disinfection and sterilization of the camp area.
After establishing the campsite, the logistics support team erected a total of 26 jumbo tents across four categories: command communication, equipment storage, medical decontamination, and living accommodation, as well as dog kennels, to ensure the provision of over 30 sets of rescue equipment at the scene.
Kim Jong-un's daughter interacts closely with his father, while his wife is left on the side.
(Kuala Lumpur, November 11th) North Korea held its 75th anniversary of the Armistice Day parade in the evening, where Kim Jong-un's daughter Kim Yo-jong not only attended but also stood on the dais with her father.
North Korean state media released footage on Sunday showing Kim Ju-ah hugging her father close, making affectionate eye contact and whispering to him several times. She gently held her father's cheek with her hands, even touching his chest. The father-and-daughter interaction was broadcast to the whole country.
However, First Lady Li Xueju could only step aside.
According to reports from "The Korean People's Newspaper" and others, on the official photo taken by Kim Jong-un and Lee Seo-ju couple on their daughter Kim Ji-ae’s 7th birthday dinner, Kim Ji-ae was seen sitting in the middle C seat, which is rarely seen. Moreover, on the 75th anniversary of the Army Day military parade the following evening, she was seen alongside Kim Jong-un on the dais together.
After the parade, North Korean state media "Koryolink" released footage that revealed more heartwarming scenes of father-daughter relationships.
Kim Jong-un looked repeatedly at his daughter in the presidential box, both of their smiles never fading. They whispered to each other in their ears. At one point, Kim Chogung embraced his father’s cheeks with both hands, and Kim Jong-un responded with a wide smile.
Other state media images show that during times when Kingmu-ae is sitting on an indoor sofa with Kim Jong-un, she constantly touches her father’s face with her hand; and when she walks alongside her father, she touches Kim Jong-un’s chest with her hand.
And the First Lady, Li Xuequ, was always at the back or to the side, always at a few steps away from her husband and daughter.
Korean media note that since Kim Jong-un first appeared in public in late November last year following his test launch of the Nodong-17 missile, his chances of appearing in public have increased over the past three months, and he has now appeared at official functions five times so far.
North Korean state media used honorifics such as "dearest heir" and "exalted heir" when mentioning Kim Chuwai, and broadcast clips of Kim Chuwai repeatedly shouting his unwavering support for white-blooded lineage while overlooking the parade from the stands.
These signs raise doubts about Kim Gu-ae’s pre-arranged succession to the Kim regime, with The Washington Post analyzing it as “a signal from Kim Jong-un elevating his middle-aged daughter to the position of successor.” However, others argue that such a conclusion is too hasty, noting that there are still various possibilities given that Kim Jong-un has a son.
"The Fund E Account" is here: The CSRC authorizes development, allowing all of an investor's funds under management to be pooled and queried - Economic Observation Net - Professional Financial News Website
Difficult to collect account information due to the complicated channels for purchasing funds?
Always forgetting about the "slush fund"?
These issues faced by farmers will soon be resolved.
February 10, the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC) announced that the "Fund E Account" APP has been launched and is currently undergoing public trial operation on various mobile app stores.
According to the introduction, the "Fund E Account" provides a one-stop service for individual investors to query information about public fund accounts and holdings, aiming to address industry pain points such as investors forgetting their accounts or finding it cumbersome to inquire.
According to data from Wind, as of the end of 2022, there were 156 fund management companies in China, managing a fund size of approximately 26 trillion yuan; there were 167 fund share registration institutions, and 411 fund sales institutions.
Each share registration institution has an independent account system and there is no industry-wide unified query channel.
Industry insiders stated that at the end of 2021, China had more than 720 million fund investors, meaning that half of the country's population had invested in fund products.
Previously, investors had to check their purchases through different sales institutions, but with the “Fund E Account,” all information about purchases from all销售渠道 can be readily accessed, making it clear at a glance what funds they hold.
"What is the 'Fund E Account' APP?"
According to relevant documents, "Fund E Account" APP is an official mobile application developed and constructed by the China Securities Depository and Clearing Corporation with approval from the China Securities Regulatory Commission, offering a one-stop query of the holdings of all market open-end fund products for investors.
Investors can conveniently and quickly track their holdings of open-ended fund shares across various channels through which they have purchased funds from different managers via the “Fund E Account,” thereby significantly enhancing the efficiency of inquiries.
Specifically, investors can query through the “Fund E Account” information including: fund account information opened with all public offering fund managers, trading account information opened with public offering fund sales institutions, and the holdings of products such as open-end shares of publicly offered securities investment funds and collective asset management plans established by securities companies where the number of investors is not subject to a limit of 200 people.
Yang Qikun, head of business for the Shanghai Securities Fund Evaluation Research Center, told the Economic Observer that investors can get all information about their ETF holdings through the "Fund E Account" app in one go, helping them recover "forgotten assets." More importantly, it enables clients to consolidate comprehensive fund investment information across accounts, allowing clients to better understand their investment situation in real time and accurately. This, in turn, helps clients optimize their fund portfolio more effectively and better plan their financial arrangements.
How do I register and use?
The reporter noted that currently, the "Fund E Account" APP has been launched in the app stores of Huawei, Apple, Xiaomi, OPPO, and vivo, but the APP is still in an open trial operation phase, requiring users to fill in an invite code to register. Investors can obtain the invite code by contacting the fund management company they hold.
A customer service staff from a mid-to-large-sized public fund management company in Shanghai provided a six-digit invitation code to an Economic Observer reporter and said, "During the beta testing phase of the app, China Securities Clearing provides each fund manager with a certain number of invitation codes. Investors can call to obtain them, and we provide them all."
Users will no longer need an invite code to register when open registration is enabled after the trial run is over.
Please provide the Chinese text that needs to be translated.
The reporter registered the account and completed the query following the 'Fund E Account' download and usage instructions posted on the website of the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC), which took only a few minutes. The process mainly consisted of four steps: user registration, real-name verification, binding of fund account, and querying public offering funds.
After completing the real-name authentication step, click the “Assets” fund binding button. All fund products purchased via various fund sales platforms by the reporter will be listed in the binding option list (accounts that can be bound). After binding is complete, one can see the total asset value of the invested funds and start using the query function.
Notably, the “Fund E Account” provides querying services for investors but does not facilitate buying or selling.
The data displayed on the "Fund E Account" usually corresponds to the date three trading days prior to the query date (T day).
For instance, on February 10, opening the "Fund E Account" displays the total assets, fund units held, and net asset value (NAV) on the assets page corresponding to the date three trading days prior, which is February 7.
