Multiple economic downturns hinder Taiwan's poor start to the year - CNET China
Xinhua Taipei, February 11 (Xinhua reporters Zhao Bo and Huang Yang) Exports suffered another five consecutive months of declines, with the manufacturing purchasing managers’ index (PMI) contracting for seven straight months, and the consumer price index (CPI) again hitting “three-digit territory”… In recent times, the authorities in Taiwan have successively released January economic data for 2023.
Experts analyze that Taiwan's economy struggled to show good performance at the beginning of the year, with considerable growth pressure.
According to the Financial Affairs Bureau of the Taiwan authorities, Taiwan’s exports in January this year were $31.51 billion, down 21.2% year-on-year and falling for the fifth consecutive month.
The export value of the 11 major export categories has declined compared to the same period last year.
Rubber and plastics, as well as their products, and optical equipment saw the steepest declines, with year-over-year reductions of 37.6% and 35.7%, respectively.
Electronics component exports fell by 20.1% year-on-year, marking the largest decline in 11 years.
Among them, integrated circuits declined 18.3% year-on-year, marking the largest drop in 14 years.
Department of Statistics Director Cai Minna said this indicates that the weakness in consumer electronics industry demand is spreading, and the electronic industry is entering a correction phase.
Statistics show that Taiwan's imports and exports both declined in January, with a trade surplus of only $2.34 billion, the lowest level in nearly three years.
The Taiwan authorities' financial affairs department believes that decreased global demand and inventory adjustments are dampening manufacturers' buying intentions, which means that the export downturn in Taiwan is likely to persist in the short term and the country's exports may fall more severely than expected in the first quarter of this year.
According to the Central Institute of Economic Management in Taiwan, the seasonally adjusted Purchasing Managers' Index (PMI) for Taiwan's manufacturing sector in January this year was 40.4%, down 3.3 percentage points from December last year and contracting for seven consecutive months.
In the economic monitoring index system, PMI has 50% as its boundary line; an index greater than 50% indicates expansionary conditions, while an index below 50% indicates contraction.
In January, five components of Taiwan's PMI contracted in new orders, production, employment, and delivery times to suppliers, while inventories tightened.
All six major industries are reporting PMI contraction, with contraction speeds in descending order as follows: electrical and mechanical equipment industry (35.1%), electronic and optical industry (35.2%), chemical and biopharmaceutical healthcare industry (39.2%), basic materials industry (42.4%), transportation equipment industry (42.6%), and food and textile industry (45.7%).
On the price front, Taiwan’s “Statistics Bureau” announced that the year-on-year increase in CPI for January this year was 3.04%, marking another breach of the 3% threshold since July last year.
Whereas vegetable prices rose 28.25%, hitting a 17-month high.
Taiwan's "Statistics Bureau" special committee member曹志弘 admitted that food price hikes have indeed exceeded expectations, excluding factors related to the Spring Festival, this year's average CPI in January and February should be close to 2.71% in December last year, inflation pressure still exists, and it remains at high levels.
Looking ahead to Taiwan’s economy this year, experts express pessimism based on reports from media such as the United Daily News and Yahoo Finance in Taiwan.
Professor Wu Daren from the Economics Department of “Central University” in Taiwan analyzed that the export downturn could cause cash flow problems for export-manufacturing firms, leading to an increased risk of default on debts.
At the same time, reduced orders lead to firms cutting labor costs, which affects the labor market and household economies, thereby impacting consumption capacity.
Dr. Chiu Dah-Shyang of the Taiwan Economic Journal Institute believes that given this year’s unresolved inflation issues in Europe and America, coupled with sustained demand decline, Taiwan’s export contraction is expected to persist throughout the first half of the year.
Due to Taiwan’s economy being supported by exports and given the current低迷 export performance, its growth for the year will be weaker than last year.
New members of the Central Committee, alternate members, and leading officials at provincial and ministerial levels complete training on studying Xi Jinping's Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China - Latest News - Hunan Daily Network - Huanasohua News Online
The Graduation of the New Members of the Central Committee, Alternate Members, and Leading Cadres at Provincial and Ministerial Levels Learning and Research Class on Xi Jinping's Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the Spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China
2023-02-11 13:07:20 [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor-in-Chief: Li Shuxue] Font size: [Large Medium Small]
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10 – The seminar for new members of the Central Committee, alternate members, and senior officials from provinces and ministries to study and implement Xi Jinping’s New Era of Socialism with Chinese Characteristics and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China concluded late today at the Central Party School (National Administration Institute). Chairman of the Political Bureau and Secretary of the Secretariat of the CPC Central Committee, Ma Xiaotian, attended the closing ceremony and delivered a closing speech.
He stated that to thoroughly study and implement President Xi Jinping’s important speech at the opening ceremony of the seminar, one must further strengthen support for “two establishments” and resolutely uphold “two maintenances,” enhance their abilities, and work diligently in practice. They should strive to advance all aspects of China’s modernization in an all-round way, achieving accomplishments that can withstand the test of history, practice, and the people in the process of comprehensively building a modern socialist society and comprehensively advancing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar, all participants guided by Xi Jinping's Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, studied in depth the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China and President Xi Jinping's opening remarks at the seminar's start. They engaged in in-depth discussions and exchanges based on actual circumstances, deepening their understanding of a series of major theoretical and practical issues concerning China's modernization. This strengthened their confidence and determination to advance the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation under the strong leadership of the Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core. It also heightened their sense of responsibility and mission to perform their duties, do their work well, and ensure a good start to the new era and new journey.
At the graduation ceremony, 10 representatives from the seminar spoke, reporting on their learning gains and exchanging experiences.
Zai Cai Qi’s statement, studying and implementing Xi Jinping’s Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China is both a primary political task in the current and future period, and a long-term strategic task. It should be carried out according to the requirement of “comprehensively learning, comprehensively grasping, and fully implementing.” This will push the work of studying and implementing these ideas to go deeper, more practically, and more deeply into people’s hearts.
To more deeply grasp the decisive significance of “two establishment,” to uphold the core position of Xi Jinping and the authority and centralized unified leadership of the Party Central Committee resolutely, and to continuously improve one’s political judgment, political insight, and political execution capabilities, always maintaining high consistency in terms of ideology, politics, and actions with the Party Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core.
To excel in mastering the Marxist theoretical foundation, to consciously arm our minds, guide practice, and advance work with the Party's innovative theories, we must put effort into deep study, meticulous understanding, and sincere practice. We need to genuinely learn for firm belief, absolute loyalty, and mission担当.
To implement in a resolute and dynamic manner the various decisions and deployments of the 20th Congress of the Communist Party of China, to advance solidly the Chinese-style modernization, to pull up our sleeves and work hard, to lower our bodies and serve as construction managers, and to turn the blueprint into reality step by step.
Always keep in mind that comprehensive strict governance of the Party is a journey that never ends and the self-revolution of the Party is a journey that never ends, tighten and solidify political responsibility for comprehensive strict governance of the Party, with Party building in terms of politics as the leading force, and advance the new great project of Party building in the new era profoundly and extensively.
To enhance our ability to promote high-quality development, serve the people, and manage and prevent risks, we must foster a strong tradition of investigation and research. We must resolutely prevent and overcome formalism and bureaucratism.
Zhai Qingfeng, Li Jianjie, Li Shulei, Chen Wenqing, Liu Jinguo, and Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony, with Chen Xi presiding over the ceremony.
VIENTIANE – VNA Special Correspondent reports that Vietnam’s Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and his spouse successfully concluded official visits to Singapore and Brunei, achieving comprehensive, pragmatic, and specific results.
During his three-day visit to Singapore and Brunei, Premier Pham Minh Chinh attended over 30 different activities.
The achievements have injected new momentum into further deepening, broadening, and enhancing both the strategic partnership between Vietnam and Laos and the comprehensive partnership between Vietnam and the EU.
During his visit to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh continued to reaffirm Vietnam’s and the Party’s foreign policy line, which is independence, diversity, flexibility, willingness to be good friends and reliable partners for all countries, and responsible members of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is each country’s need, aimed at enhancing the well-being of its people, and committed to peace, stability, and development in the region and the world.
At various talks, President范文政 consistently agreed with his counterparts from Singapore and Brunei to enhance political mutual trust through visits of high-level delegations, effective implementation of bilateral cooperation mechanisms, and important memorandums of understanding through such means.
Many cooperation documents were signed during this visit.
Among them, the Memorandum of Understanding on a Green and Digital Economy Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei from 2023 to 2027 are highlights.
Vietnam signs Memorandum of Understanding on Partnership in Green and Digital Economy with Singapore.
From Vietnam News Agency
During meetings with business leaders, seminars, and economic forums, Premier Pham Minh Chinh emphasized that Vietnam welcomes and creates favorable conditions for Singapore and Brunei enterprises to expand their investment scope in areas such as digital transformation, green energy, high-tech, and innovation and creativity in Vietnam.
This visit not only helps to deepen cooperation between Vietnam and Singapore and Brunei in traditional areas such as politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defense, education and training, oil and gas, tourism, people-to-people exchanges, but also creates frameworks for cooperation in new potential areas such as digital economy, green economy, energy transition, innovation and creativity, smart cities, and sustainable development.
Brunei’s Sultan Hassanal Bolkiah and Prime Minister Pham Minh Duty are about to enter a bilateral discussion session.
The image is from VNA.
During his visits to both countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh made time to visit and listen to the concerns and aspirations of the Vietnamese community residing there.
During their leaders' meeting, Premier Pham Minh Chinh suggested that both countries’ authorities pay more attention to ensuring fair treatment for the local Vietnamese community, provide them with opportunities to contribute to local society, and create favorable conditions to foster relations between the two countries.
All of these proposals were agreed to and supported by leaders from both countries.
Specifically, Premier Pham Minh Chinh shared with their counterparts the desire for a united, peaceful, stable, and prosperous ASEAN Community; agreeing to maintain unity and collaboration with ASEAN countries and enhance ASEAN’s central role in regional and complex international situations.
With important achievements from his official visits to Singapore and Brunei, Premier Pham Minh Chinh contributed positively to effectively implementing Vietnam’s Thirteenth Party Congress priority of strengthening relations with ASEAN neighbors, effectively implementing the 12th Political Bureau Conclusion of the Communist Party of Vietnam on New Era Vietnamese Diaspora Work (12-KL/TW), and mobilizing the strength of the entire nation.
(The End)
What exactly was "the object" that was shot down over Alaska?
Confused, speculation abounds.
The US military shot down a unidentified object flying over Alaska near its coast on Friday afternoon (February 10th) using the US' most advanced stealth fighter jet, the F-22.
The spot where it was shot down is ten miles off the Alaskan coast.
This is the second time American military has downed an airborne object in less than a week.
Last Saturday, a Chinese spy balloon drifted over American airspace for several days before being destroyed near the coast of South Carolina in the United States.
The Pentagon said that the second object shot down was first detected entering US airspace on Thursday night, while it was moving in the northeastern part of Alaska, tracked by US military forces. It flew at an altitude of 12,000 meters (40,000 feet), about the size of a small car, much smaller than the Chinese spy balloon shot down previously.
The Pentagon also believes there is no indication at this time that the object is manipulatable.
John科比, Coordinator for Strategic Communication at the National Security Council, stated on Friday that while the object is flying at high altitudes and its exact appearance is unclear, it “poses a reasonable threat to the safety of civilian aircraft.”
Kobe stated that the object is different from the spy balloon discovered in the United States, which did not have a payload hanging from it.
Kobe said, “We refer to it as an ‘object’ is the best description we can make at this moment.”
President Biden consulted with the Pentagon before ordering the object to be shot down, and he made this decision “very carefully,”科比 added.
The official description of this object by the US authorities can be summarized as follows: about the size of a small car, without control sticks, without suspension systems, and flying at an altitude of around 10,000 meters.
But these pieces of information still fail to address fundamental questions such as what this object is, which country it belongs to, and what task it is performing.
Currently, many analyses and speculations online suggest that this could be another Chinese balloon.
It could be that both the spy balloon intruding into US airspace and the Chinese balloon floating over Latin America are from China, each performing some task in different locations.
Some have linked this "object" from Alaska to unidentified flying objects (UFOs).
The report by US Newsweek quotes a tweet from US former Representative Peter Meijer on Friday saying, "I wish this unidentified flying object was also a spy balloon instead of a legitimate UFO."
The irony of equating extraterrestrial spacecraft with weather balloons is amusing, but that does not warrant an interstellar conflict, Marks said.
Margett made this tweet shortly after Kobe confirmed that the object in Alaska had been downed.
The Weekly said that it was not just Major Gray who doubted the object to be a UFO.
Republican Representative Tim Burchett of Tennessee criticized the government's cover-up of intelligence last month and demanded that the Office of the Director of National Intelligence release reports on "unidentified flying objects."
Iran marks Revolution anniversary as hackers attack President's televised speech in support of protesters
The Islamic Republic of Iran held an official rally Saturday to commemorate the 44th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, but anti-government hackers briefly interrupted President Ebrahim Raisi’s televised speech.
The president’s televised speech was interrupted on the internet for about a minute, with the logo of a group of cyberhackers opposing the Iranian government appearing on the screen. The group’s name is "Edalat Ali (Ali Justice)."
Another voice shouted “Death to the Islamic Republic.”
According to a report today by Reuters, hackers disrupted coverage of a national TV station in Iran as the country commemorated the anniversary of the revolution.
Iranian officials mark the 44th anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, as the hardline government of Rouhani faces the boldest challenge from young protesters demanding their ouster, but Rouhani nonetheless calls on "misled youth" to repent so they can receive pardons from Iran's highest leaders.
Protests swept across Iran following the death of 22-year-old Mahsa Amini, who died in custody by the country's morality police in September.
Iranian security forces carried out deadly crackdowns on protests, which is one of the strongest challenges the Islamic Republic has faced since the revolution in 1979 that overthrew its 2500-year-old monarchy.
As part of a campaign amnesty for the anniversary of the Revolution, Iranian authorities released on Friday Mahsa Hafizi, an imprisoned dissident who had gone on a hunger strike, and Fariba Adeli, an Iranian-French academic.
Earlier, Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei issued a decree of amnesty that includes some prisoners arrested in recent anti-government protests.
According to the human rights group HRANA, as of Friday, 528 protesters have been killed, including 71 minors.
It is reported that 70 government security personnel were killed.
It is believed that up to 19,763 protesters were arrested.
For weeks, Iranian leaders and official media have been calling for voting at Saturday’s rally to show opposition to the protests and support for the government.
On the Friday night celebrating the anniversary of the Iranian Revolution, official media showcased fireworks as part of government-sponsored celebrations, and people shouted "Allahu Akbar!" (God is greatest!)
(God is the greatest!)
However, one can also hear many people shouting "Death to the dictator!" at the rally.
And ‘the Death of the Islamic Republic’ videos posted on social media.
On Saturday, government television broadcast live footage of official rallies across the states.
In Tehran, as part of official celebrations,国产 ballistic missile interceptors, drones, anti-submarine cruisers, and other military equipment were showcased.
President Lee's speech was often interrupted by chants of "Fuck America" – a标志性chant at these state rallies.
The crowd still shouted "Death to Israel."
Reuters said that Adelkhah, who has been in prison since 2019 and is one of seven French nationals detained in Iran, is one of the factors contributing to the deteriorating relations between Paris and Tehran in recent months.
She was sentenced to five years' imprisonment in 2020 for charges of national security.
Later they confined her at home, but in January she returned to prison.
Adelkhah denies these allegations.
And just a week before Mesa was released, supporters warned that he was at risk of death due to his hunger strike.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting mandatory headscarves.
The French Ministry of Foreign Affairs released Adelkhah on Friday and called for her release, including allowing her to return to France if she wishes.
