On March 29, I purchased this book through pre-order for 31 yuan, and it showed that it would be pushed to my device on March 31st. At this time, the Amazon website was still unavailable for previewing the book because it had not yet been released.
On March 31, the book sent to the device is blank with only "coming soon," while the electronic version of the book on Amazon has been discounted to 18 yuan.
For two days, I repeatedly attempted to delete the blank books downloaded from the device and resynchronize, but was unable to obtain the electronic version of "The Essence of Business" that contains actual content. However, I noticed that the book is already available for preview on Amazon's website.
Currently, I have a few impressions.
The issue of price is not the most crucial one; rather, the key is how to replace the blank books on Kindle with books that actually have content, rather than always downloading books that say "coming soon."
The books purchased on pre-order should not be bought again, after all, downloading a book with no content due to delay would seem very complicated in terms of procedures.
