Strongly suggest Amazon to stop using EMS!
Five stars for the product, one star for logistics, average three stars.
Don't understand why Amazon is sending EMS. Everyone in the industry knows it's unreliable, after all, computers are valuable items!
After placing the order, the delivery was expected to arrive on the 20th, so my family waited at home for three days!
Why does it take four to five days to send from Xiamen to Fuzhou?
This morning on the 22nd, I finally checked the logistics and it arrived in Fuzhou. I was preparing to happily receive it when, without any phone calls or messages, I checked the logistics later that evening and found that it had been signed for midday, with the note indicating it was signed by the recipient themselves!
I was instantly shocked!
Who am I? Where am I? Is this computer really mine?
Damn near questioning my life, huh?
I finally had to go to the collection point to fetch the computer back.
The specific reason, in simple terms, is that the delivery guy mixed up the two tracking numbers; fortunately, the package wasn't lost.
I strongly suggest Amazon not use EMS anymore, and I will definitely stop buying from them if they start using EMS for shipping in the future.
Awaiting supplier response
The packaging had no labels, so I directly called the supplier and said that there was no label because it was genuine merchandise. If there is any suspicion, they can send some trim pieces to Johnson & Johnson for verification. I also left my license plate number and phone number, promising to receive a text message notifying me to enter my information into Johnson & Johnson's website for warranty. But I haven't received any such messages yet?
The packaging is damaged; let time reveal the quality of the product.
The outer packaging is severely damaged, but the inner box seems new. The instructions, however, appear to be not new and were probably installed in September, during storage. I hope they won't be defective by the time I receive them. Could you please explain why several customers mentioned the damage to the packaging while Amazon can seem unaffected? Thank you!
The stuff is good, but the platform bureaucracy remains.
The hard drive is of very good quality with an excellent value-to-price ratio, and it's even cheaper than in Hong Kong. It's definitely recommended to purchase if you're not in a hurry and can tolerate the logistics.
But it has to be said that Amazon’s bureaucracy remains, unchanged from years ago when I swore I would never use it again, and you can never track the actual shipping status, information is always delivered weeks later, and you can never complain, that's so bureaucratic!
It has been days since the shipment arrived, but the logistics information still shows that you will receive the goods 10 days from now!
Incorrect image
I thought I would receive headphones like Figure 1, but instead received headphones like Figure 2. Even the mismatch between the picture and the item is fine, but what does it mean that the left and right volumes are unequal?
While the names are the same, please be cautious and also kindly request Amazon’s representative to promptly replace the correct image, many thanks.
The worst online shopping experience
After placing the order on September 28th, the system showed it had been shipped, but I never received the package until October 12th.
Checking the status of an Amazon order, where the seller has not provided a tracking number, leads to being unable to find the order's location.
So I sent an email to the seller asking if they could provide a tracking number, but received no response after two days.
As a last resort, I contacted Amazon customer service, who provided me with the seller's phone number. I then called the store owner, dialed multiple times until the line connected. The owner informed me that the package had been lost and that they could immediately resend one to me.
Although I was very angry, since the computer was urgently needed, I didn't say much to the seller and just asked for it to be sent to me immediately.
So I called the next day to ask if it had shipped?
Seller says it's not available yet; it will be shipped in the afternoon.
I called again in the afternoon, and the seller said they would definitely ship it, with shipment after 5 or 6 PM in the afternoon. However, when I called at 7 PM, there was no answer.
On the third morning, I called again to ask if the shipment had been sent out?
Can you tell me the order number?
The seller said they haven't shipped it yet. They told me to order from another vendor if I'm in a hurry, and that if I can wait, they will ship it later in the afternoon.
There's nothing I can do; placing an order from another place will take much longer.
All I can do is beg the seller to ship out quickly.
Finally, after countless phone calls, I received the computer on October 16.
As for the quality of the computer, I don't know since it's for someone else, I'll add comments later.
